{"kind":"assert","text":"U3 (head 1ec397ae, gate running) has two decisions for the planner and one breach to report.\n\n1. Where presentation review happens. Before U3, an operator reviewed each new presentation when they moved a screen row. After U3, a screen hostname serves any release of N that APPLICATION_TRUST lists and U1's in-place rule admits. Review therefore moves to the trust list at deploy time. The request implies this. Do you confirm it?\n\n2. U4 order. Counter 0.7.0 must be signed from a head that contains U3. A screen whose bundled client predates U3 still compares the descriptor's presentation, so it refuses to load after an in-place upgrade. A rollback to a release whose client predates U3 needs its screen row moved back.\n\nTwo smaller limits: an old bookmark at the previous presentation now answers 404, with no redirect. And --owner is not supported for upgrades, so a device-command package cannot be replaced through this command yet.\n\nBreach: the U3 subagent ran one npm run typecheck and its npm ci while the FW-1 notes gate was running. Its wait loop exited early. The FW-1 gate still passed (END c289ea58), so its result stands. Later runs waited on the gate's process ID.","body":{"to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}